      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "dc:source": "trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act.pdf, p.54",
      "skos:note": "A term of a consumer contract is unfair if it causes a significant imbalance in the parties' rights and obligations, is not reasonably necessary to protect legitimate interests, and would cause detriment to a party.",
